  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Police cooperation Colombia - development of new project</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Polissamarbete Colombia - upparbetning ny fas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">M&#xe5;let med det h&#xe4;r projektst&#xf6;det &#xe4;r att Svenska Polismyndigheten (SPA) ska identifiera omr&#xe5;den f&#xf6;r eventuellt fortsatt samarbete med den colombianska polismyndigheten (CNP), och utveckla en projektans&#xf6;kan som ska l&#xe4;mnas in till Sida. Sida har gett st&#xf6;d till samarbete mellan SPA och CNP sedan 2013, genom 2 olika projektfaser (fas 1 2013-2017 och fas 2 2018-2023). Vidare kommer s.k. &quot;bryggaktiviteter&quot; att finansieras f&#xf6;r aktiviteteter som SPA genomf&#xf6;r tillsammans med CNP p&#xe5; plats i Colombia.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project support is for the Swedish Police Agency (SPA) to identify areas for possible continued cooperation with the Colombian National Police Agency (CNP), and to develop a project application to be submitted to Sida. Sida has provided support for collaboration between SPA and CNP since 2013, through 2 different project phases (phase 1 2013-2017 and phase 2 2018-2023). Furthermore, so-called &#x201d;bridging activities&#x201d; will also be implemented, which SPA will carry out together with CNP on site in Colombia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this contribution is for the Swedish Police Agency (SPA) to identify areas for possible continued cooperation with the Colombian Police Agency (CNP), and to develop a project application to be submitted to the Embassy. The Embassy in Bogot&#xe1; has supported cooperation between SPA and CNP since 2013, through 2 different project phases (phase 1 2013-2017 and phase 2 2018-2023). Identification of cooperation areas for a third phase will take place in close cooperation with the Colombian Police Agency.

Furthermore,  so called bridging activities will be financed for activities that SPA carries out together with CNP on site in Colombia.</narrative>
  </description>
